### Bridge inbound path — deposit hardening + second live proof (cc63065a86)

End-to-end testing of the ETH->AIT deposit leg found and closed real defects:

- **Self-send mint hole fixed**: any tx whose sender is the bridge wallet
  is skipped (self-sends and the bridge's own outbound sends are never
  deposits). Before this, the ETH_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY holder could mint AIT
  payouts for gas. Proven live: self-send 0xb431fc7f33a82e9ce1227bacb37cc3c1fe3a6e13931f464587fabb6b111a034e
  (Sepolia block 11807841) scanned and ignored — no row, no payout.
- **External-sender proof**: fresh wallet 0xE7Bb3a334C372239349918C9D0F760E48e18B6A6
  deposited 0.0015 ETH in Sepolia tx 0x6d7434a8d1dc843782466aec51b801d9063f39f115d65e3be7b3d3a66df4eb38
  (block 11807830); credited 527232857 units (14.645357 AIT) to canary
  0x992b2241da9918845bf32d1249bf53eaaa761d06 via payout tx
  0x643659a0c319883fbb194b8c2655d894909b0042f9869eb989b7e951420121b8 at
  AITBC block 28092 — verified on all five hosts. The earlier 14.5556-AIT
  canary credit (block 28032) was a self-send test artifact, not a backed
  deposit.
- **Confirmation depth**: the monitor now scans only blocks buried by
  BRIDGE_CONFIRMATIONS (default 3; raise to >=12 for mainnet). A reorg of
  an unconfirmed deposit can no longer undo a paid payout.
- **Retry taxonomy**: temporary failures — oracle outage, RPC error,
  missing stored price — stay PENDING_RETRY and recompute at retry time;
  FAILED is reserved for permanent problems (no recipient, below minimum)
  and retry exhaustion, all logged at CRITICAL with an ALERT marker
  (funds received but not paid must never be silent).
- **Oracle staleness**: Chainlink answers older than
  CHAINLINK_MAX_AGE_SECONDS (default 3 days — Sepolia feeds are sparse
  test data) are treated as unavailable, which now retries the deposit.
- **Float alert**: each poll critical-logs ALERT when the payout wallet
  drops below BRIDGE_LOW_FLOAT_AIT (default 50) so deposits stop piling
  up in PENDING_RETRY unnoticed.
- **Duplicate monitor disabled by flag**: the wallet app's embedded
  deposit watcher now requires BRIDGE_DEPOSIT_MONITOR_ENABLED=true
  (default off). It had BRIDGE_ENABLED=true from exchange.env on hub and
  node2 — two independent watchers would double-pay the day both hold
  keys. Per the key-split plan this component never gets a payout key.
- **fleet-config-check**: new sections assert exactly one live deposit
  monitor, display the hub payout config (AIT_USD_FIXED_PRICE, address,
  minimums), and FAIL on ETH_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY carriers beyond
  aitbc-wallet (the withdrawal payer). Current exposure: 13/11/8 carriers
  on hub/hub1/node2 via blockchain-secrets.env — confinement tracked as a
  pending operational item (requires restarting the shared-secrets
  carriers, incl. the hub proposer).
- **Stranded deposits settled**: 0x746aebaf... (0.05 ETH, Sep 26, no
  recipient — permanent failure) refunded on the ETH side minus gas via
  Sepolia tx 0x18867d5dd8bc79ed467cebbe011d62c1098d81a9ba71adb1e08dae9d9e0248b5
  (block 11807877). hub1 ledger row 0x36470037... (0.01 ETH, Aug 31,
  recipient recorded, never paid — legacy pending state) was settled by
  crediting the recorded 84.854 AIT to 0x1d8B34f249b96169E48E956b00c307898FbaF087
  via payout tx 0xc07d9eb4db0d49737a8a27eb63338b709a8a1220a718400e3d80b2d6df65f688
  (AITBC block 28101). Policy: refund ETH-side when no AIT recipient was
  encoded; pay the recorded AIT credit when one was.

