### feat(ops): replay-chain --checkpoint — seed state at a checkpoint DB, verify, replay C+1..end (V-5)

- `scripts/ops/replay-chain.py` gains `--checkpoint DB`: a state-bearing chain.db whose tip C seeds the replay target wholesale (the equivalent of a node that stopped at C resuming sync). Three proofs gate the first import — lineage (checkpoint head hash == snapshot block C, and C+1 names it parent), state-bearing (the checkpoint's account table recomputes to block C's recorded state_root, same input set as `compute_state_root_full`), and a post-`init_db` re-seed root check (catches ensure_bond_accounts-style seeding mutations). `--genesis` is unused in checkpoint mode.
- `--to-height` now actually bounds the run: the stub RPC caps the head/range it serves at the requested height instead of importing to the real tip and failing the expected-count check.
- `--compare-state-with DB` adds the V-5 ladder's layer 2: after a clean replay to the next checkpoint's tip, every non-history table is compared wholesale — covering aux consensus state (escrow, chain_parameter, bridge rows, contracts) that the account-only state root never sees. Volatile locally-stamped columns (`created_at`/`updated_at`) and the replay-generated undo journal are excluded; the compare DB's tip must equal the replay end.
- `tests/unit/test_replay_chain.py`: 29 cases — arg parsing, stub capping, checkpoint head reading, all proof failure modes (tip≥end, lineage/fork mismatch, missing root, empty accounts, root mismatch), copy placement, and wholesale-compare semantics incl. aux-table divergence and volatile-column exclusion.
- `docs/ops/v5-replay-inventory.md`: recipe updated to the implemented flags (`--checkpoint` + `--snapshot`; the planned `--from-height` did not get implemented — the checkpoint file's own tip is the start height and cannot disagree with its state).

